# Privacy Policy

**Effective Date:** November 4, 2026

## 1. Overview

PaperRepair ("we," "us," "our," or "Company") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our website and services.

**Key Principle:** PaperRepair is a **browser-based, client-side document processing tool**. This means your files are processed directly in your browser and are NOT sent to our servers.

---

## 2. Information We Collect

### 2.1 Files You Process
- **Processing Location:** Your browser (client-side only)
- **Retention:** Files are deleted immediately after processing
- **Storage:** Files are never uploaded to our servers
- **Backup:** No backups of your files are created

### 2.2 Automatic Information
When you visit PaperRepair, we automatically collect:
- **Browser Information:** Browser type, version, and user agent
- **Device Information:** Device type, operating system
- **Usage Analytics:** Pages visited, features used, time spent
- **Technical Data:** IP address (anonymized), referral source
- **Cookies:** Session cookies for functionality (no tracking cookies)

### 2.3 Information You Provide
- **Email:** Only if you voluntarily contact us for support
- **Feedback:** Any comments or suggestions you submit
- **Error Reports:** Technical errors encountered during use

---

## 3. How We Use Your Information

### 3.1 Primary Uses
- Provide and improve our services
- Process your document conversion requests
- Fix bugs and improve performance
- Respond to support inquiries
- Comply with legal obligations

### 3.2 Analytics & Improvement
- Understand how users interact with PaperRepair
- Identify popular features and tools
- Monitor system performance and uptime
- Detect and prevent abuse

### 3.3 Security
- Detect and prevent fraudulent activity
- Protect against cyberattacks
- Maintain system integrity

---

## 4. Data Security

### 4.1 Client-Side Processing
- All file conversions happen in your browser
- No files are transmitted to our servers
- Your files never leave your device

### 4.2 Transmission Security
- All connections use HTTPS (TLS 1.2+)
- Certificate pinning on supported browsers
- HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS) enabled

### 4.3 Server Security
- Security headers implemented (CSP, X-Frame-Options, etc.)
- Regular security audits
- Vulnerability disclosure program
- No sensitive data stored on servers

### 4.4 What We Don't Do
- ❌ Never sell your data
- ❌ Never share your files with third parties
- ❌ Never process files on our servers
- ❌ Never create backups of your files
- ❌ Never track you across other websites
- ❌ Never use invasive analytics

---

## 5. Cookies & Local Storage

### 5.1 Essential Cookies
- Session cookies for authentication
- CSRF protection tokens
- Preference settings

### 5.2 Analytics Cookies
- Google Analytics (anonymized)
- Conversion tracking (if applicable)

### 5.3 Local Storage
- Recent files list (your browser only)
- User preferences and settings
- Document conversion history

**Your Control:** You can clear cookies and local storage anytime in browser settings.

---

## 6. Third-Party Services

### 6.1 Analytics
- **Google Analytics:** Anonymous usage statistics
- Data shared: Anonymized page views, conversion events
- [Google Privacy Policy](https://policies.google.com/privacy)

### 6.2 File Processing Libraries
- **jsPDF, XLSX, pdfjs-dist:** Process files locally in your browser
- No data is sent to external services
- All processing happens on your device

### 6.3 Content Delivery
- **Google Fonts:** For typography
- **CDN:** For faster asset delivery
- No files or personal data shared

---

## 7. Your Rights

### 7.1 Access & Portability
You have the right to:
- Request what personal data we hold about you
- Export your data in a portable format
- Delete your account and associated data

### 7.2 Opt-Out
- Disable cookies in your browser settings
- Opt out of Google Analytics tracking
- Request data deletion (contact us below)

### 7.3 Do Not Track (DNT)
We respect DNT signals. If your browser sends DNT:
- Analytics tracking is disabled
- No tracking cookies are set

---

## 8. Children's Privacy

PaperRepair is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from children under 13. If we become aware that a child under 13 has provided us information, we will delete such information immediately.

